# Oneself in Russian: себя, сам, свой
subtitle: "Masha buys herself a jacket, chooses it herself and takes her own bag: себя, сам and свой in Russian."
tags: ["russian","себя","свой","reflexive pronoun","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/reflexive-pronoun"]
thumb: "band \"Buying for yourself, in Russian\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Flying in Russian: лечу or летаю?","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/116-russian-fly.cast"}

